; A signature returning a type variable no parameter mentions.
;
; `conjure` promises `forall a. Int -> a`. In a sound system that is
; inhabited only by non-termination: the callee cannot have produced a
; value of a type the CALLER picks. Here it is inhabited by a machine
; word, so the promise is an unchecked coercion wearing a polymorphic
; spelling - and the caller's choice is never witnessed by anything.
;
; It is not a theoretical gap. Measured on the compiler before this
; diagnostic existed:
;
;     (strWrap (conjure 42) 8)
;
; `check` answered OK and the binary exited 139 - 42 dereferenced as a
; String pointer. The same shape reaches through `vecGet`, because a
; `Vec` carries no element type, which is how a Vec holding an Int
; reads back as a String.
;
; `witnessed` is the control and must stay silent: `a` appears in a
; PARAMETER, so the caller supplies a value of it and the choice is
; witnessed by the argument. That is ordinary parametric polymorphism
; and it is sound.
;
; `declared` is the other control. Fourteen declarations in this
; repository really are raw word reads - `memGetWord`, `vecGet`,
; `nodeA` - and `;@axiom:raw` is how one says so. The tag is not
; permission and does not make the read safe; it makes the unsafe layer
; finite and enumerable, which is what `#raw` in AXSYM is for.
(:: conjure (-> Int a))

(fn (conjure n)
  (cast a n)
)

(:: witnessed (-> a a))

(fn (witnessed x) x)

;@axiom:raw
(:: declared (-> Int a))

(fn (declared n)
  (cast a n)
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
